# Configuration Guide

This minimal project has three main configuration files:

```text
.env               private local values; never commit it
docker-compose.yml starts one QKT daemon container
qkt.config.yaml    QKT runtime behavior for local strategy work
```

## .env

The generated values are enough for a first local run:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
QKT_STARTING_BALANCE=10000
```

`QKT_IMAGE_TAG` selects the QKT Docker image. `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE` is the
local account balance used by generated examples and config defaults.

## docker-compose.yml

Compose starts one `qkt` service. There is no live broker in this template.
That makes it useful for learning the CLI, testing strategy files, and building
custom integrations.

## qkt.config.yaml

The generated config uses local/default runtime settings. It does not connect to
MT5 or any other live venue.

## State

QKT writes local runtime state under `./state`. You can delete it during local
experiments, but do not treat that habit as safe for live deployments.
